PATCH 365 -- FUN_0000_902c (objtype-0x02 per-frame UPDATE method) object base-loss.  902c is the exact
structural twin of FUN_0000_7c1d (patch 244): a c0e5-dispatched (patch 243) per-object update whose object
arrives in param_1 (DI) but which Ghidra read from param_4 (a dropped register -> uninitialised) -> every
*(param_4+off) deref hit a wild host address.  On the DEFAULT native AZER1 ACCEPT COOP flow (setarch -R,
FIST_COOP_TICK=1) this is the c0e5->c0ca->902c crash the wm-mission-divergence session pinned; with the
wasm op-0x50 spin gone (patch 364) both targets converge on this path.  Same base-loss class as patches
244/335-340.  Fix (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0x902c; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00; CS=0):
  - param_4 re-pointed at the object host pointer g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)param_1 (the DI c0e5 threads);
    the whole body + the sub-method calls (912d/90cd/9176/875f/a358/a0a4/91b8/a57a/a9ea) are
    object-relative and become correct verbatim.
  - the two CS-relative indirect-call tables rebased to g_mem + threaded with DI: asm 0x9060
    `call *cs:0x90a0(bx)` (bx=byte[di+0x3d]&0x1e) and asm 0x906a `call *cs:0x91a7(bx)` (bx=byte[di+0x3e]).
    Ghidra emitted the first as a raw offset (-0x6f60=0x90a0) and mis-based the second onto DGROUP
    (&DAT_2000_51a6); both are CS=0 code-segment tables -> g_mem+0x90a0 / g_mem+0x91a7.
Mirrors patch 244 verbatim (bases substituted).  NOTE: 91b8 (reached from 902c) carries its own 7e29-class
weapon-table base-loss (`byte[di+0x91]*2 + -0x6dfa`), pinned as a separate member.

